    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d242">

                <pb facs="0598" n="576" xml:id="pg576"/>

                <head>No. 107.<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">Earl Granville to Lord
                    Tenterden.</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Foreign Office</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1872-06-12"><hi rendition="#italic">June</hi> 12,
                        1872</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#center">[From British Blue Book “North America,” No. 10, (1872,) p.
                    2.]</p>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">My Lord</hi>: Sir Roundell Palmer having consented,
                    at the request of Her Majesty’s Government, to attend the meeting of the
                    Tribunal of Arbitration on the 15th instant as Her Majesty’s Counsel, I have to
                    instruct you to be guided by his advice in all your proceedings.</p>
                <p>I am, &amp;c.,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>GRANVILLE.</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
